    "result_text": "All 288 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, the application now counts how many other owners already share that owner's last name and returns it as the integer field `namesakeCount` in the owner response.\n\nI followed the existing pattern already used for the other creation-time computed fields (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `membershipTier`):\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (and MapStruct's auto-mapping) picks it up.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes `countNamesakes(lastName)` from the currently-registered owners (the new owner isn't persisted yet, so it's naturally excluded) via exact last-name match, and sets it before saving.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`** \u2014 added `createOwnerReturnsNamesakeCount`, asserting the first owner with a given last name gets `0` and a second sharing it gets `1`.\n\nNote: `namesakeCount` is computed as the count of *other* existing owners with the same last name at the moment of creation, using exact-equality matching (the plainest reading of \"same last name\"), consistent with how the sibling creation-time fields work.",
